# C++ conventions

- Standard: **C++20** (not C++23)
- Headers: `#pragma once` (not include guards)
- No namespaces
- Classes: `CamelCase`; methods/vars: `camelCase`
- Interfaces: `FooI` suffix (`EntityI`, `ScreenI`, `DrawerI`, …)
- One primary type per `.hpp` / `.cpp` pair, side by side under `src/<area>/`
- Gameplay tick: `EntityI::update(float dt)` / `ScreenI::update(float dt)` — `dt` in seconds (fixed timestep)
- Screen transitions: `ScreenUpdaterI::{push,pop,replace}Screen` (deferred scene stack)

## Includes

- From `src/`: angle brackets — `#include <entities/Paddle.hpp>`
- Same directory: quotes — `#include "EntityI.hpp"`
- Prefer existing interface headers over reaching into concrete SFML types from screens

## Style (match `.clang-format`)

- LLVM-based, 4 spaces, column 120, `PointerAlignment: Left`
- `SpaceBeforeParens: Never` → `if(`, `for(`, `while(`
- Braces on new lines (`BreakBeforeBraces` / `BraceWrapping`)
- Warnings as errors (`-Wall -Wextra -pedantic -Werror` / MSVC `/W4 /WX`)

After larger edits: `cmake --build --preset debug --target format` (Debug configure required).
